{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1537626-amkhata-familiar","id":1537626,"title":"Amkhata Familiar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-18T10:56:38-07:00","id":1537626,"title":"Amkhata Familiar","content":"Could a mage have an Amkhata as a Familiar given that it is an Ephemeral Entity? If so, which Arcana would be used to forge the bond? They seem to exist on the deathly frequency of Twilight so Death seems like it would do the trick. On the other hand, they are Sekhem-adjacent beings so perhaps relating it to an aspect of the Five-Fold Soul and then using the Subtle Arcana that it roughly corresponds to could be thematically fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T13:49:03-07:00","id":1537634,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand Amkhata, yes it would be Death Arcana, but (and my understainding is limited) Amkhata are totally focused on getting Sekhem and cannot manifest without it. They would only want to bond w/ a mage (if it is possible) if the mage could help them get Sekhem. and I did not think Mages could directly affect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T22:57:29-07:00","id":1537642,"title":"","content":"Amkhata dematerialize when they run out of essence, a mage could transfer it daily trough the familiar link.<br /> It would simply be a little more expensive (rank*essence daily) than a normal familiar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T03:04:07-07:00","id":1537644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1537626-amkhata-familiar?p=1537634#post1537634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand Amkhata, yes it would be Death Arcana, but (and my understainding is limited) Amkhata are totally focused on getting Sekhem and cannot manifest without it. They would only want to bond w/ a mage (if it is possible) if the mage could help them get Sekhem. and I did not think Mages could directly affect that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are correct for the most part, though the writeup for Wilfried Moeller in the Mummy 2e Core does seem to somewhat imply that Amkhata do have a psychology beyond just hunting Sekhem. I'd probably equal them to a particularly intelligent predator rather than the sapient-adjacent beings like a ghost or spirit. So a mage would have to keep them on a tight leash and keeping it from simply following its instincts would probably be pretty difficult. And indeed mages can't directly affect Sekhem, though they can mess with Pillar Points and a mage could create a Vestige using the same Rite sorcerers use, so they would have some tools to negotiate with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T03:05:04-07:00","id":1537645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1537626-amkhata-familiar?p=1537642#post1537642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amkhata dematerialize when they run out of essence, a mage could transfer it daily trough the familiar link.<br /> It would simply be a little more expensive (rank*essence daily) than a normal familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though they could also just have the Amkhata hang out in Twilight rather than keeping it manifested. Or only manifesting it when there is a reason to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T06:02:37-07:00","id":1537651,"title":"","content":"Given that Amkhata are mentioned as distinct from ephemeral beings in a couple places, use a completely different manifestation process with an unusual interaction with the phase of Neter-Khertet, largely lack the intelligence to make the willing agreement necessary to become and remain a familiar, and are incapable of engaging with Mummy's closest equivalent to the Familiar bond (they can't hold Pillars), my reading would be that you can't use the Familiar rules for connecting with an Amkhat any more than you can a Hedge ghost or a qashmal.<br /> <br /> You could gin up something roughly similar in effect with Creative Thaumaturgy, but it wouldn't be any variation of the Familiar spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T10:34:02-07:00","id":1537660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1537626-amkhata-familiar?p=1537651#post1537651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Amkhata are mentioned as distinct from ephemeral beings in a couple places, use a completely different manifestation process with an unusual interaction with the phase of Neter-Khertet, largely lack the intelligence to make the willing agreement necessary to become and remain a familiar, and are incapable of engaging with Mummy's closest equivalent to the Familiar bond (they can't hold Pillars), my reading would be that you can't use the Familiar rules for connecting with an Amkhat any more than you can a Hedge ghost or a qashmal.<br /> <br /> You could gin up something roughly similar in effect with Creative Thaumaturgy, but it wouldn't be any variation of the Familiar spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! So out of curiosity, what do you imagine a Creative Thaumaturgy 'not-familiar' bond with an Amkhata would look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T15:07:20-07:00","id":1537663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1537626-amkhata-familiar?p=1537660#post1537660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! So out of curiosity, what do you imagine a Creative Thaumaturgy 'not-familiar' bond with an Amkhata would look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest issue is that Amkhata are notably absent from the biggest Mage/Mummy crossover rules text and the Arcana are notably not the primary division of spell effects in Awakened magic \u2014 Practice-wise it's probably reasonable to assume most of the sense-sharing and Essence-transmission effects would be Patterning or Ruling, but given the established difficulties of handling Sekhem and the complications of transferring Pillars anything resembling the familiar bond on an Amkhat would likely be the product of multiple spells and/or come with its share of complications, possibly represented with effects mechanically equivalent to Paradox Conditions a la being killed in the Astral by the Ecstatic Wind or messing with a loyal mummy's Name.<br /> <br /> Basically if you're doing anything more involved than meshing your vision and/or throwing Essence and/or Pillar points at it I would expect some of its bestial nature to bleed into you, whether as murderous hunger or mutative twists of the flesh; I'd compare it to becoming the master of one of the Geryo from Werewolf in terms of occult bleed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}